            description: "Fruit Notes describes Crimson Gold, Svatava Cv., as a Czech Republic scab-resistant apple available from Adams County Nursery and tested in Massachusetts beginning in 2011. Source notes: hard crunchy fruit with high acid and high sugar, complex sweet-tart flavor, bright red-orange blush over yellow, medium-large size when adequately thinned, 3 to 3.5 inch diameter, around 20 lb firmness, Brix often about 14 and sometimes up to 16, little pre-harvest drop, green-white crisp-melting flesh, somewhat chewy skin, medium-vigor upright-spreading trees, biennial risk without thinning, possible cider use, fresh-eating recommendation, and ANIFIC descriptors of fine texture, juicy aromatic fruit, 13 Brix, 17.6 lb pressure, and 7 to 8 month storage life"
